  "text": "Sarah Lyles, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology) - MedVet\nFor Pet Parents\nFor Veterinarians\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFind a Clinic\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nFind a Clinic\nReferral Partner Login\nRefer a Patient\nLocations\nFind A Doctor\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nReferral Partner Resources\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFor Pet Parents\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFor Veterinarians\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nRefer a Patient\nFind a Doctor\nSarah Lyles\nSarah Lyles, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nBoard-Certified Veterinary Oncologist\nSarah Lyles, DVM, Diplomate, ACVIM (Oncology), is a\nBoard-Certified\nMedical Oncologist\nat both\nMedVet Mandeville\nand\nMedVet New Orleans\n.\nDr. Lyles attended Louisiana State University in Baton Rouge, LA, where she earned a Bachelor of Science in Biological Sciences and Louisiana State University School of Veterinary Medicine where she earned a Doctor of Veterinary Medicine degree.\nFollowing her graduation from veterinary school, Dr. Lyles completed a yearlong internship in small animal medicine and surgery in Virginia-Maryland Regional College of Veterinary Medicine in Blacksburg, VA, a yearlong oncology internship at Florida Veterinary Specialists and Cancer Treatment Center in Tampa, FL, followed by a three-year residency in small animal oncology at the University of Florida College of Veterinary Medicine in Gainesville, FL.\nSince becoming a board-certified Diplomate of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine, Dr. Lyles has been published articles on various oncology topics in multiple veterinary journals including the\nJournal of Veterinary Emergency and Critical Care\n,\nVeterinary Clinical Pathology\n, and The\nJournal of Veterinary Internal Medicine.\nShe is also an active advocate of continuing education for veterinary professionals and has lectured on a variety of oncology topics.\nAlthough Dr. Sarah Lyles is experienced in all aspects of small animal oncology, she has particular interest in the treatment of hemangiosarcoma and lymphoma. She  is dedicated to  supportive client communication and compassionate care.  When not treating patients, Dr. Lyles enjoys swimming, yoga, photography, and spending time with her family and dogs.\nEducation & Training\nBachelor of Science:\nLouisiana State University, Baton Rouge, LA\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine:\nLouisiana State University, Baton Rouge, LA\nInternship (Rotating Small Animal Medicine and Surgery):\nVirginia-Maryland Regional College of Veterinary Medicine, Blacksburg, VA\nInternship (Medical Oncology):\nFlorida Veterinary Specialists and Cancer Treatment Center, Tampa, FL\nResidency (Medical Oncology):\nUniversity of Florida, Gainesville, FL\nSpecializations\nBoard Certification:\nDiplomate of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Oncology)\nAssociations\nAmerican College of Veterinary Internal Medicine\nVeterinary Cancer Society\nAmerican Veterinary Medical Association\nLouisiana Veterinary Medical Association\nSpecialties\nMedical Oncology\nServicing Locations\nMedVet Mandeville\nMedVet New Orleans\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to know our specialists better and to show you why we love our team members so much! Meet Dr. Sarah Lyles, a Board-Certified Medical Oncologist at both MedVet Mandeville and MedVet New Orleans.\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to know our specialists better and to show you why we love our team members so much! Meet Dr. Sarah Lyles, a Board-Certified Medical Oncologist at both MedVet Mandeville and MedVet New Orleans.\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
